1
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:09,050
A lift can carry at most 630 kilograms.

2
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,110
A delivery worker weighs 80 kilograms.

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:16,280
She wants to take boxes of 25 kilograms each.

4
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:19,350
What is the largest number of boxes she can take?

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,760
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:22,810 --> 00:00:26,740
80 plus 25 B must be less than or equal to 630.

7
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:30,470
So 25 B is at most 550, and B is at most 22.

8
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,840
She can take up to 22 boxes.

9
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:37,790
Any number up to 22 works, so the answer is a range.

10
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:44,090
Remember: less than, less than or equal to, greater than, and greater than or equal to.

11
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:46,980
Solve an inequality just like an equation.

12
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:49,950
The solution set is every value that works.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,220
Show it on a number line.

14
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:57,910
Use an open circle for less than, or greater than: that value is not included.

15
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:58,620
Your turn.

16
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:00,680
X is less than or equal to 3.

17
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:03,660
Does the circle at 3 look open, or closed?

18
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:06,270
Pause and choose.

19
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,130
A closed, filled-in circle.

20
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:11,840
3 is included, so it is less than or equal to.

21
00:01:11,890 --> 00:01:17,610
When you multiply or divide both sides by a negative number, reverse the sign.

22
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:18,970
Here is the method.

23
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:21,940
Step 1: solve it like an equation.

24
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:27,120
Step 2: if you multiply or divide by a negative, reverse the sign.

25
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:32,260
Step 3: show it with open or closed circles, or list the integers.

26
00:01:32,310 --> 00:01:34,930
Step 4: check with a value.

27
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:38,720
Solve 7 minus 2 X is greater than or equal to 13.

28
00:01:38,770 --> 00:01:41,430
Take 7: negative 2 X is at least 6.

29
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:47,630
Divide by negative 2, and reverse: X is less than or equal to negative 3.

30
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,400
Your turn.

31
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,850
Solve negative 3 X less than 12.

32
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,930
Pause and work it out.

33
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:57,230
Divide by negative 3, and reverse the sign.

34
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,450
X is greater than negative 4.

35
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,600
Check with X equals 0: 0 is less than 12.

36
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:03,530
True.

37
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:10,510
List the integers where negative 5 is less than or equal to 3 N plus 1, which is less than 10.

38
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:13,470
Take 1 from each part, then divide by 3.

39
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:17,590
N is from negative 2, up to but not including 3.

40
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:20,560
Jo solves 10 minus 3 X is greater than 4.

41
00:02:20,610 --> 00:02:22,560
Which line is wrong?

42
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:23,760
Line 2 is wrong.

43
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:27,400
Dividing by negative 3 reverses the sign.

44
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:28,780
X is less than 2.

45
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:32,880
Check with X equals 0: 10 is greater than 4.

46
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:37,830
Weight limits, speed limits and budgets are inequalities, not equations.

47
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:40,860
Anything up to the limit is allowed.

48
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,170
One last question.

49
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:45,740
What is the largest integer with 2 X less than 9?

50
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:49,100
Pause the video and answer.

51
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:50,700
X is less than 4.5.

52
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:54,200
The largest integer below 4.5 is 4.

53
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:58,110
To remember: solve inequalities like equations.

54
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:02,690
Multiplying or dividing by a negative reverses the sign.

55
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:05,620
Open circles for less than or greater than.

56
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:09,040
Closed circles when the value is included.

57
00:03:09,090 --> 00:03:11,300
Check with a value.

58
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:16,430
Great work! Now practise lesson 4.3 on Camday.
